  ],
  "text": "Carry a set of scales to the top of Everest and you lose weight instantly. Nothing about you changed. Same body, same bones, same breakfast. Gravity gets weaker the further you are from the centre of the Earth. And a summit puts eight extra kilometres between you and that centre. So the needle drops by about a third of a percent, and the scale is not broken. But the mountain is not even the strange part. The Earth is not a sphere. Spinning has left it fatter around the middle. So standing in Ecuador puts you further out than standing in Norway. Your weight was never really a fact about you. It is a measurement of whatever is underneath you. And almost nobody knows what is actually down there. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
